# harmony-closure-spine.rows — vendor-official.sh SPINE_OURS assignment
# (the W-SESS spine closure copy list), machine-spliced by
# gen-staging-emit-closure.mjs; the staging-generated gate fails on drift.
# Same rules as harmony-closure.rows: literal rows are policy (must exist
# under runtime/dsh), `@walk` lines re-expand from the pin trees. The
# pre-flip two-group accumulation (SPINE_OURS="$SPINE_OURS\n…") is
# absorbed into this one list — identical shell value, one block. The
# SPINE_PKG_DSH roster stays in the script (the machine-read interface
# gen-staging-manifests.mjs parses); the MOBILE preset docs and npm faces
# stay in their script-side stage blocks.
